eed to compute \\(F(F(z))\\) and higher compositions to see if there is a repeating pattern.\n\n#### Compute \\(F(F(z))\\):\n\\[ F(F(z)) = F\\left(\\frac{z+i}{z-i}\\right) \\]\nLet \\(w = \\frac{z+i}{z-i}\\), then:\n\\[ F(w) = \\frac{w+i}{w-i} \\]\nSubstitute \\(w = \\frac{z+i}{z-i}\\):\n\\[ F\\left(\\frac{z+i}{z-i}\\right) = \\frac{\\frac{z+i}{z-i} + i}{\\frac{z+i}{z-i} - i} \\]\n\nSimplify the numerator and the denominator:\n\\[ \\text{Numerator: } \\frac{z+i}{z-i} + i = \\frac{z+i + i(z-i)}{z-i} = \\frac{z+i + iz - i^2}{z-i} = \\frac{z+i + iz + 1}{z-i} = \\frac{z + iz + i + 1}{z-i} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Denominator: } \\frac{z+i}{z-i} - i = \\frac{z+i - i(z-i)}{z-i} = \\frac{z+i - iz + i^2}{z-i} = \\frac{z+i - iz - 1}{z-i} = \\frac{z - iz + i - 1}{z-i} \\]\n\nThus:\n\\[ F\\left(\\frac{z+i}{z-i}\\right) = \\frac{z + iz + i + 1}{z - iz + i - 1} \\]\n\n#### Simplify further:\nTo simplify, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ \\frac{z + iz + i + 1}{z - iz + i - 1} \\cdot \\frac{z + iz - i + 1}{z + iz - i + 1} \\]\n\nAfter simplifying, we find:\n\\[ F\\left(\\frac{z+i}{z-i}\\right) = -\\frac{1}{z} \\]\n\n#### Compute \\(F(F(F(z)))\\):\n\\[ F(F(F(z))) = F\\left(-\\frac{1}{z}\\right) = \\frac{-\\frac{1}{z} + i}{-\\frac{1}{z} - i} = \\frac{-1 + iz}{-1 - iz} = \\frac{1 - iz}{1 + iz} = \\frac{1 - iz}{1 + iz} \\]\n\n#### Compute \\(F(F(F(F(z))))\\):\n\\[ F(F(F(F(z)))) = F\\left(\\frac{1 - iz}{1 + iz}\\right) = \\frac{\\frac{1 - iz}{1 + iz} + i}{\\frac{1 - iz}{1 + iz} - i} = z \\]\n\nThus, \\(F(F(F(F(z)))) = z\\), indicating that the function \\(F\\) has a period of 4.\n\n### Step 3: Determine \\(z_{2002}\\)\nSince the sequence is periodic with period 4, we compute \\(2002 \\mod 4\\):\n\\[ 2002 \\mod 4 = 2 \\]\n\nThus, \\(z_{2002} = z_2\\).\n\n### Step 4: Compute \\(z_2\\)\nWe already have:\n\\[ z_1 = F(z_0) = F\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) \\]\n\\[ z_2 = F(z_1) = F\\left(F\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right)\\right) \\]\n\nFrom the periodicity, we know:\n\\[ z_2 = F(F(z_0)) = -\\frac{1}{z_0} \\]\n\nGiven \\(z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i\\):\n\\[ z_2 = -\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{137} + i} \\]\n\nRationalize the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = -\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{137} + i} \\cdot \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} - i}{\\frac{1}{137} - i} = -\\frac{\\frac{1}{137} - i}{\\left(\\frac{1}{137}\\right)^2 + 1} = -\\frac{\\frac{1}{137} - i}{\\frac{1}{18769} + 1} = -\\frac{\\frac{1}{137} - i}{\\frac{18770}{18769}} = -\\left(\\frac{1}{137} - i\\right) \\cdot \\frac{18769}{18770} \\]\n\nThus:\n\\[ z_2 = -\\left(\\frac{1}{137} - i\\right) \\cdot \\frac{18769}{18770} = -\\left(\\frac{18769}{137 \\cdot 18770} - i \\cdot \\frac{18769}{18770}\\right) = -\\left(\\frac{1}{137} - i\\right) \\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[ z_{2002} = \\boxed{-\\left(\\frac{1}{137} - i\\right)} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-\\left(\\frac{1}{137} - i\\right)}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
